"intro": "**Ivy Chen**, the head gardener (black bob, round red glasses, olive overalls); the trustees **Fay Morgan**, **Gus Patel** and **Cal**, who has moved abroad; the beneficiaries, the **Owusu siblings**, all adults. Shift change at the bothy! The Owusu trust of the garden cottages has three trustees: Fay, Gus and Cal. Let's see who hangs up an apron...",
"steps": [
{
"say": [
{
"who": "Britney",
"text": "Cal has moved to Canada. He's been there over a year now."
},
{
"who": "Fay",
"text": "Can we replace him?"
}
],
"q": "Does the power to appoint a new trustee in Cal's place arise?",
"opts": [
"Yes. He has remained outside the UK for more than 12 months (s.36(1)).",
"No. A trustee can only be replaced if he dies.",
"Only if Cal agrees in writing.",
"No. Living abroad never matters."
],
"a": 0,
"why": "That is one of the s.36(1) grounds.",
"whys": [
"",
"s.36(1) lists several grounds, including more than 12 months outside the UK.",
"Replacing him under s.36(1) removes him without his consent.",
"More than 12 months outside the UK is a ground."
]
},
{
"say": [
{
"who": "Ivy",
"text": "No one is named in the trust deed to appoint new trustees. So who chooses?"
}
],
"q": "Who can appoint Cal's replacement?",
"opts": [
"Fay and Gus, the continuing trustees, in writing (a deed in practice).",
"The Owusu siblings, by telling Ivy.",
"Only the court.",
"Cal's personal representatives."
],
"a": 0,
"why": "Named, next, nearest: with no one nominated, the continuing trustees appoint.",
"whys": [
"",
"A beneficiaries' direction under TLATA s.19 must be in writing and by all of them; here the trustees can act.",
"The court steps in only where it is impracticable without it.",
"They act only after the last surviving trustee dies."
]
},
{
"say": [
{
"who": "Britney",
"text": "Years later, only Fay and Gus are trustees. Fay wants to retire and nobody will replace her."
},
{
"who": "Fay",
"text": "Can I just retire by deed under s.39?"
}
],
"q": "Can Fay retire under s.39?",
"opts": [
"No. Only one person (Gus) would be left; s.39 needs two persons or a trust corporation to remain.",
"Yes, as long as Gus consents by deed.",
"Yes, and she is then free of any liability for the past.",
"Yes, if she gives a month's notice."
],
"a": 0,
"why": "She must find a replacement under s.36 or ask the court.",
"whys": [
"",
"Consent is needed, but two persons or a trust corporation must also remain.",
"She would stay liable for breaches while she was a trustee.",
"There is no notice rule; the s.39 conditions are not met."
]
},
{
"say": [
{
"who": "Britney",
"text": "The Owusu siblings are all adults and together absolutely entitled. They write to the trustees naming their cousin as the new trustee."
}
],
"q": "What lets the siblings do this?",
"opts": [
"TLATA 1996 s.19: no one is nominated to appoint, they are all of full age and capacity and together absolutely entitled, and they all direct in writing.",
"s.36(6), because they are beneficiaries.",
"Nothing: beneficiaries can never choose trustees.",
"A direction by any one of them is enough."
],
"a": 0,
"why": "Before 1996, Re Brockbank meant they could not force a choice.",
"whys": [
"",
"s.36(6) is for the nominated person or existing trustees adding trustees.",
"That was the position before TLATA s.19.",
"All the beneficiaries must direct (s.21)."
]
},
{
"say": [
{
"who": "Ivy",
"text": "The appointment is made by deed. Do we need to transfer everything by hand?"
}
],
"q": "What does the deed do?",
"opts": [
"It vests most of the trust property in the trustees automatically (s.40), but the shares need a transfer registered by the company, and registered land needs registering at HM Land Registry.",
"It moves everything automatically, shares included.",
"Nothing: a deed is only evidence.",
"It only works for land."
],
"a": 0,
"why": "Most keys fly over; some stay on their hooks.",
"whys": [
"",
"Shares and stock are an exception (s.40(4)).",
"A deed of appointment vests most property automatically.",
"It vests most kinds of trust property."
]
}
],
